    "body": "Question for the maintainer (part 1, transport on Windows). This question does not block the work.\n\n- On Linux and macOS, part 1 uses a Unix domain socket from std. No network port opens.\n- On Windows, std has no named pipe and no local socket. Thus part 1 binds TCP on `127.0.0.1` only, with a port that the OS selects. A random token in the discovery file gates each connection.\n- A named pipe on Windows needs one of these dependencies:\n  1. `windows-sys` (already in `Cargo.lock` through `camcraft-post`) as a new direct dependency of `camcraft-app`, with the `Win32_System_Pipes` feature. This option needs `unsafe` FFI code.\n  2. The `interprocess` crate. It is not in `Cargo.lock` now.\n- Recommended: option 1, in a follow-up PR. Only the `not(unix)` arms of `crates/app/src/mcp/link.rs`, `wire.rs` and `link_client.rs` change.\n\nUntil you decide, the loopback port with the token stays. The decision file `docs/decisions/3751-cli-ui-link.md` records this.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
