    "body": "Part 1 (the `--ui` transport) is on issue/3751-cli-ui · PR #3861 (draft, `Refs #3751`) · pinned by `egui_app::tests::ui_link::a_cli_ui_call_shows_in_the_window_and_ctrl_z_removes_it`, `mcp_live` `ui_link::a_cli_call_with_no_window_says_so_and_exits_3`, `ui_link::a_wrong_token_is_refused_and_the_window_goes_on_serving` · merges at the next cut.\n\nWhat part 1 delivers:\n- Each window opens a UI link at start. Linux and macOS use a Unix domain socket. Windows uses TCP on `127.0.0.1` only, until the named-pipe dependency question above has an answer. `CAMCRAFT_UI_LINK=off` disables the link.\n- A discovery file `<pid>.json` in the user's link folder names the window, its open project and a random token. Each connection must send the token first.\n- `camcraft-cli --ui [--window <pid|project>] call <tool> [<json>]`, `--ui mcp` and `--ui windows`. The window runs each call on its own History through the MCP tool surface. Ctrl+Z undoes it.\n- With no window, the CLI exits 3 and runs nothing. It never falls back to headless mode.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/3751-cli-ui-link.md`.\n\nWhat remains:\n- Part 2: `camcraft-cli --skill <folder|claude|copilot> install`.\n- `--ui script` is the follow-up #3850.\n\nI released the claim. Part 2 is free to claim.\n",
