    "body": "Security review of the UI link (PR #3861, read from `origin/main` 16115cd06). The review is read-only. No build was done.\n\n1. Loopback only: ok. The link binds `Ipv4Addr::LOCALHOST` (`crates/app/src/mcp/link.rs:223`). The `--mcp-port` listener also binds it (`crates/app/src/mcp/listen.rs:154`).\n2. Token: ok, with a note. The token is 256 bits of SipHash output under `RandomState` keys that std seeds from the OS random source (`link.rs:95-110`). The secret part is the 128-bit key, so the strength is 128 bits. Std does not document `RandomState` as a CSPRNG. The compare is constant time for tokens of the same length (`link.rs:121-129`). A wrong or missing hello closes the connection before a line reaches the app (`listen.rs:319`, `listen.rs:330-334`).\n3. Discovery file: ok. The file has the token (`link.rs:53`). On Unix the folder is 0700 (`link.rs:196-204`) and the file is 0600 (`link.rs:235-239`). On Windows the file is in `%APPDATA%`, which only the user, SYSTEM and Administrators can read by default. The code sets no ACL of its own.\n4. Socket file: ok on Unix. The socket is 0600 in a 0700 folder (`link.rs:206-219`). It is removed on a normal exit (`link.rs:159-168`, the inbox drops when `run_windowed` returns). Gap on Windows: a stale file of a crashed window lets another local user bind the stale port and act as the window to the CLI. Filed as #3874 (P3).\n5. Size limit and timeouts: 16 MiB line cap, 5-minute idle drop, 5 s write deadline (`listen.rs:56-68`). The UI thread only parses lines in `mcp_host::pump` and does not wait. Gap: the same 5-minute window and 16 MiB cap apply before the token check, so a client without the token can hold the only session. Filed as #3873 (P3).\n6. No unwrap, expect or panic on the request path: ok (`listen.rs`, `wire.rs`, `link.rs`, `link_client.rs`, `crates/ui/src/mcp_host.rs`). A dropped client is logged (`listen.rs:245`, `listen.rs:117-121`).\n7. Same command path: ok. Link requests go through `answer_live_with` with the same `LiveGate` as `--mcp-port`, on the window's History (`crates/ui/src/mcp_host.rs:24-30`, `:43-66`).\n\nNo P1 was found. No other user can run a command in the window, and no request can crash the UI.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
